# .claude/ is ignored EXCEPT skills/.
#
# The PR-review skill has to be committed: claude-review.yml checks out the
# repo and loads .claude/skills/codetrellis-pr-review by name, so an ignored
# skill means the reviewer silently falls back to generic findings.
#
# Note `.claude/*` and not `.claude/` — git cannot re-include a path whose
# parent directory is excluded, so the trailing-slash form would make the
# negation below do nothing.
#
# Everything else under .claude/ stays local: settings.local.json holds
# per-machine permissions, worktrees/ holds working copies.
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

test-results/
marketing-assets/test-results/
playwright-report/
.playwright-mcp/
.codetrellis/

# E2E harness — per-test working dirs (cloned fixture + tmp data dir).
# The harness creates these in setup and deletes them in teardown;
# any leftovers after a crash are safe to wipe by hand.
#
# Underscore prefix (not dot prefix): the file watcher's ignore
# function skips any path segment starting with `.`, which would
# silently neutralise the fixture inside.
tests/_tmp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Private security working notes. NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC. docs/private/ holds the Phase 19 finding
# register: unremediated vulnerabilities with file paths and line numbers.
# Publishing that is an exploitation roadmap for software running on
# developer workstations with network reach into adjacent systems.
#
# Safe to publish: the architectural rules the findings produced (they read
# as standards). Not safe: severities, reproduction detail, or which sink is
# still open. Those live here and stay here.
#
# ci.yml enforces this — a tracked file under docs/private/ fails the build.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/private/
